  "music": "w4-castle-clatter",
  "authorNotes": "Solo. Two identical lever-gate-swing units back to back, over a real moat this time (void hazard beneath everything past the starting pier). Pull lever-w4-02-a (latching) to raise door-w4-02-a, then grab swing-w4-02-a (pivot 880,640, 260px reach) to cross the first gap to the checkpoint pier. Repeat the pattern: lever-w4-02-b raises door-w4-02-b, swing-w4-02-b (pivot 1630,610, 250px) carries you to the goal pier. Both signal pairs are direct producer-to-consumer (lever->door), no relay involved — this level is still purely about learning that a gate now guards a real fall, not about combining anything new. Grab camera-w4-02 near spawn for the photo objective (allAirborne, easiest mid-swing). Both gaps carry an assist beam for players who'd rather not trust the swing at the usual Clock cost. The checkpoint sits on the middle pier so a missed second swing doesn't cost the first gate."
